// @test: verify-fail
// @tier: 0
// @level: L1
// @tags: refinement, quantifiers, forall, exists, substitution, capture, soundness
// @timeout: 30000
// @expected-error: proof-failed

/// A quantifier that binds the refinement's own name must SHADOW it.
///
/// Substituting a value into a refinement predicate walks the predicate
/// replacing the refinement variable. That walk had explicit rules for
/// `block`, `if`, `match`, `closure` and `for`, and none for `forall` or
/// `exists` — so a quantifier fell through to the structural walk, which
/// rebuilds a node with every child substituted and knows nothing about
/// what the node binds. The quantified variable was rewritten.
///
/// Both types below are UNINHABITED under the correct reading and
/// INHABITED under capture, which is what makes this file a test rather
/// than a demonstration:
///
///   `forall x in 0..3 => x == 7` quantifies its own `x`, so it asks
///   whether every one of 0,1,2,3 equals 7. It does not. Capture turns it
///   into `forall x in 0..3 => 7 == 7`, which is true of everything.
///
/// So a function claiming to return one of these must NOT verify. Before
/// the fix it did — or, in a debug build, tripped the `debug_assert!` that
/// stood in for a scope rule and killed the verifier outright. Release
/// builds delete that assertion, so there the capture simply happened.
///
/// This went unnoticed because the whole `verify-pass` / `verify-fail`
/// category ran a typecheck and reported PASS without ever calling a
/// verifier (T0957). The assertion was written, and nothing asked it.
///
/// Task: T0958. The companion `quantifier_shadow_still_substitutes.vr`
/// holds the other half: refusing to substitute everywhere would satisfy
/// this file and prove nothing.

/// The quantifier binds `x`, shadowing the refinement's `x`.
type ForallShadow is x: Int where forall x in 0..3 => x == 7;

/// The same for the existential.
type ExistsShadow is x: Int where exists x in 0..3 => x == 7;

@verify(formal)
public fn forall_shadow_MUST_FAIL() -> ForallShadow {
    7
}

@verify(formal)
public fn exists_shadow_MUST_FAIL() -> ExistsShadow {
    7
}

mount core.prelude.*;

fn main() {
    print("a quantifier shadows the refinement variable");
}
